'' A nested call must not eat the outer call's arguments. The callee's extent into the
'' shared argument pool was opened BEFORE its arguments were lowered, so 'F( G( 7 ), 9 )'
'' emitted 'call void F(%4, %5)' -- F( 7, G(7) ) -- and dropped the 9 entirely. No
'' decline, no diagnostic, wrong arguments.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/nestedargs.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: %5 = call i32 G(%4)
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void F(%5, %6)
